.TH FASTRDP-CHECK-HOST 8 "October 2026" "fast-rdp-server" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fastrdp-check-host \- check a fastrdp host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastrdp-check-host
.RB [ \-\-preflight ]
.br
.B fastrdp-check-host
.RI [ user ]
.br
.B fastrdp-check-host \-\-ports
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints one line per check:
.B ok
or
.B FAIL
(and
.B warn
for what to check by hand). Run it as root. The exit status is 1 when a check failed.
.TP
.B \-\-preflight
Before the setup: supported release, the host name is the FQDN and resolves to the
real address, DNS SRV records of the KDCs (with dig), time synchronisation, ports
3389 and 3390 free, fastrdp-server and its nftables table, and
.BR "fastrdp-defaults status" .
.TP
.I user
On a set-up host: services, listeners (xrdp on loopback only), broker and token
sockets, nftables table, TERMSRV keys, Kerberos and SSSD ticket renewal, proxy module and
FreeRDP, xrdp, the broker configuration, time; with a directory
.I user
also NSS, the PAM account check and the user's ticket. Then
.B fastrdp-defaults status
and
.BR "fastrdpctl status" .
.TP
.B \-\-ports
Print the proxy and xrdp ports read from the configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fastrdp-defaults (8),
.BR fastrdpctl (8),
docs/manual-setup.md
